* Boats catch creatures stepping off the dock (openc2e Creatures 2 project,
* our own script). Run by openc2e after the world loads (Additions folder);
* safe to repeat.
*
* The east boat (3 6 1) moors right against the end of the dock (its left
* edge at x 6560; the dock ends at 6565), the west boat (3 6 2) against its
* docks the same way, so a creature stepping off the end fell straight
* through the boat into the sea (owner, 2026-11-12: "the creature should land
* safely in the boat if they walk off the dock and the boat is there").
*
* A hidden watcher (2 1 155) looks every 2 ticks: a creature whose middle is
* over a boat at rest (not rowing: OV01 0, no speed) and whose feet have
* dropped below the boat's top by more than 6 px (off the dock, falling)
* but not past its bottom is taken aboard (GPAS, as boarding does), and the
* boat is sent across at once, the way its own timer would send it (activate
* 1 from the west mooring, activate 2 from the east). The timer alone runs
* only every 1200 ticks (2 minutes), so a creature caught this way sat in
* the moored boat that long, with nothing to do: a passenger's mind waits
* for the ride to end (owner's screencast 2026-11-13 15:55, the west boat).
* The transit pod (3 6 3) is not a boat and is left out.
* A creature is caught up to 40 px short of the boat's near end too: one
* stepping off the east dock's end (x 6565) has its middle about 20 px west
* of the moored boat's edge (6560-6600), so it fell past the boat into the
* gap, its middle landed in the sealed water under the dock (room 31), was
* lifted back and stepped off again (30 of 36 room 31 rescues in a 5-minute
* test run, 2026-11-15). (The search for the boat to board below still
* matches it by its own left edge, var0.)
*
* The east dock's end (room 13 to 140, x 6565) is open to creatures only
* while the east boat is moored against it (2026-11-14): otherwise a creature
* stepping off it fell into the gap above the sea, its middle landed in the
* sealed water under the dock (room 31), the engine lifted it back onto the
* dock's end, and it stepped off again: 43 times in 16 minutes, one creature
* 18 times (some norns' genes make "west" walk east, so its mind never saw
* the drop ahead). At 150 the doorway is too small for a creature (224).

enum 2 1 155 kill targ next
inst
new: simp blnk 1 0 0 0
setv cls2 2 1 155
setv attr 16
mvto 5000 1320
tick 2
slow

scrp 2 1 155 9
  inst
  setv var7 0
  enum 3 6 1
    doif ov01 eq 0 doif velx eq 0 doif posl gt 6540 doif posl lt 6600
      setv var7 1
    endi endi endi endi
  next
  doif var7 eq 1
    setv door 0 13 140 255
  else
    setv door 0 13 140 150
  endi
  enum 3 6 0
    doif spcs ne 3 doif ov01 eq 0 doif velx eq 0
      setv var0 posl setv var1 posr setv var2 post setv var3 posb
      setv var4 0
      setv var8 var0 subv var8 40
      enum 4 0 0
        setv var5 posl addv var5 posr divv var5 2
        doif var5 gt var8 doif var5 lt var1
          setv var6 var2 addv var6 6
          doif posb gt var6 doif posb lt var3
            setv var4 1
          endi endi
        endi endi
      next
      doif var4 eq 1
        enum 3 6 0 doif posl eq var0 doif post eq var2
          gpas
          doif spcs eq 2
            doif posl le 340 mesg writ targ 0 endi
            doif posr ge 1040 mesg writ targ 1 endi
          endi
          doif spcs eq 1
            doif posl lt 6745 mesg writ targ 0 else mesg writ targ 1 endi
          endi
        endi endi next
      endi
    endi endi endi
  next
endm
